      "title": "System-library allowlist accepts directory traversal",
      "message": "The system-library allowlist checks only the raw prefix. A Mach-O dependency such as /usr/lib/../../opt/vendor/libcustom.dylib passes this check despite resolving outside the permitted system directories. The package can therefore be marked verified while retaining an unbundled external dependency, breaking relocation and potentially loading unintended code.",
      "suggestion": "Reject parent-directory components before accepting system-library paths, or normalize the dependency path before checking that it remains within an allowed system directory.",
